// 2026-07-19: Terminal I/O FFI. Replaces Print#/PutChar# intrinsics.
// !Print(x)/!PrintLn(x) dispatched by print plugin (Mid stage).
//
// 2026-09-09 (Family A+B, briev-native runtime): the print family frgns are
// REMOVED — the symbols (__print_int, __print_float, __print_char,
// __print_bool, __eprint_str) are now pure-Briev defns in
// lib/std/cast_lanes.bv (write(2) via SysCall#, float_format for %.9g), and
// the backend's emit_declares declare-guard skips them. Keeping an frgn here
// would (a) declare a symbol the defn defines and (b) keep pulling
// briev_rt.o into every link for symbols the C file no longer contains.
//
// __print_float64 stays C-backed for now (the f32-only float_format engine
// does not yet cover doubles); it is declared by emit_declares and resolved
// from briev_rt.c when a program actually prints a Float64.
// Undo: restore the frgn lines from git history if the defns regress.
